B.djW=new A.q("tapBehavior",B.bD,"tapopen-0830 (BINDING fleet UX standard) + house rule 7a: tapping a card ALWAYS OPENS it \u2014 a generic detail surface with the card's full content \u2014 the configured `action`/`onTap` if set, else the engine's own detail surface. tapfull-0831: on phone that surface is a PUSHED full-screen route (app bar + back), never a slide-up bottom sheet; on desktop/wide it is a full-view centered dialog (house rule 7a \u2014 the old right side-sheet is retired). Set \"expand\" (LEGACY value, kept for source compat) to also guarantee the inline expand-in-place chevron is shown (see `expandChevron`) without needing to opt into it separately \u2014 the body tap itself still OPENS either way; expand-in-place is reachable ONLY via the chevron icon, never the body (house rule 7a: one tap, one outcome).",B.bET,null)
B.d5N=new A.q("expandable",B.W,"Whether this card can expand inline at all (default true). Set false for a card with nothing to expand \u2014 no chevron renders.",B.f,null)
B.dgq=new A.q("expandSingle",B.W,'LEGACY (`tapBehavior: "expand"` only): opening a card collapses its siblings \u2014 at most one card expanded at a time (a card mid-edit keeps its editor).',B.f,null)
B.d75=new A.q("expandChevron",B.W,'Shows the expand affordance as an explicit trailing chevron icon (44px hit box) under the default `tapBehavior: "open"` \u2014 the body tap opens the item; only the chevron toggles the inline `expandFields` preview. Under `tapBehavior: "expand"` the chevron is ALWAYS shown (this prop is a no-op there, since expand-in-place has no other affordance once the body tap opens) \u2014 house rule 7a: the card body tap always opens, expand is reachable only via an explicit icon.',B.f,null)
B.QI=new A.q("height",B.ah,"Optional fixed height.",B.f,null)
B.bEX=s(["outlined","elevated","flat","feature"],t.s)
B.da_=new A.q("variant",B.bD,"Card treatment (defaults to the style): outlined, elevated, flat, feature.",B.bEX,null)
B.d9S=new A.q("action",B.X,"Open-record action spec { fn, args }.",B.f,null)
B.d_n=new A.q("cardActions",B.X,"ALWAYS-VISIBLE per-row icon button(s) in the card's title row \u2014 no swipe, no long-press, no expand needed (unlike `swipeActions`, reveal-on-gesture only, or `openActions`, expanded-card only). List of { icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals? }: with `column` set, the button is gated against THIS row's own value (shown only when it equals/notEquals the given value); omitted `column` = always shown. `label` may be a {lang: text} map and is used as the button's tooltip. Each fires its `action` spec on the row through the normal dispatch (chains included). Use for a discoverable \"add without opening\" affordance on a live list, e.g. a search-results card whose row tap reads the item but whose `cardActions` entry saves it \u2014 gated `notEquals` the row's own \"already saved\" flag so a saved row shows its state instead.",B.f,null)
B.deo=new A.q("longPressActions",B.X,"Press-and-hold action menu \u2014 same entry shape/gating as `cardActions` (List of { icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals? }). When present (non-empty), it REPLACES the engine's built-in Open/Edit/Delete long-press menu for this node; absent, long-press keeps showing that built-in menu. Either way the popup opens as an anchored contextual dropdown AT the touch point (longpress-anchored-0831), never a slide-up sheet.",B.f,null)
B.dh_=new A.q("rowMenuExtras",B.X,"Same gated entry shape as `cardActions`/`longPressActions` (List of { icon, label, action, column?, equals?, notEquals?, destructive? }), but APPENDS to the engine's built-in Open/Edit/Delete long-press menu (between Open and Edit) instead of replacing it \u2014 use this when a node wants ONE more contextual action alongside the built-in menu rather than a full custom replacement (rowmenu-extras-0903). An entry with `destructive: true` (e.g. a replacement Delete) renders in the theme's error color, same as the built-in Delete, and is moved to the END of the menu regardless of its position in this list \u2014 non-destructive extras stay between Open and Edit in author order, destructive ones sort after the built-in Delete (rowmenu-extras-destructive-0912).",B.f,null)
B.d_M=new A.q("builtinDelete",B.W,"Set false to suppress the engine's own row Delete everywhere it would otherwise appear \u2014 the \u22ee overflow menu, the long-press row menu, AND the default \"delete\" swipe entry, all three at once (default true, exact prior behavior when omitted). Use when the applet declares its OWN guarded delete (e.g. confirms an item count, refuses when shared) so a more-discoverable built-in Delete can't bypass it and orphan data.",B.f,null)
B.df_=new A.q("expandFields",B.X,'Extra "label: value" rows shown when a card is expanded. List of { column, label?, format?: currency|percent|compact|relative|number, decimals?, prefix? } \u2014 `format` renders the value as a number, or (`relative`) humanizes an ISO-8601 timestamp column as "3m ago"/"2h ago"/"3d ago".',B.f,null)
B.d3g=new A.q("expandDetail",B.X,"A child node rendered INLINE when a card is expanded, with the row's id injected (and the cards `table` unless the node sets its own). Lets a row edit in place \u2014 e.g. a notepad or embed \u2014 with no popup.",B.f,null)
B.d2O=new A.q("expandHeight",B.ah,"Fixed height for `expandDetail` (default 340). Set it for an embed that needs a bounded canvas.",B.f,null)
B.deJ=new A.q("contentSurface",B.W,"Render expandDetail on a clean opaque surface so the card tint can't dim an embedded widget/note (default true; set false to opt out).",B.f,null)
B.dfs=new A.q("expandFit",B.W,"Size `expandDetail` to its content instead of the 340 default \u2014 a short note stays short (the child must self-size, e.g. an autoHeight notepad or an embed with its own height).",B.f,null)
B.d36=new A.q("editToolbar",B.W,"An expanded card opens with a compact control row \u2014 an optional `toolbarLead` node, an edit pencil (\u2713 to finish, \u2717 to cancel-and-revert) and a \u22ee options menu \u2014 and `expandDetail` opens read-only until the pencil turns edit on (the `editing` flag flows in).",B.f,null)
B.deu=new A.q("toolbarLead",B.X,"A node rendered at the LEFT of the edit toolbar, row-bound (e.g. a `pick` content-type dropdown).",B.f,null)
B.dkw=new A.q("menuActions",B.X,'Extra \u22ee menu items [{ label, icon?, action }] fired with the row injected (e.g. "Add subtask"); a built-in Delete is always present.',B.f,null)
B.d9o=new A.q("expandExtra",B.X,"A SECOND inline node below `expandDetail` when expanded, row-bound and content-fit (e.g. a nested cards filtered to this row's children \u2014 a subtask sub-thread, or a box's packed items). Filter it with value \"$rowId\" (the parent's internal id) or \"$parentField:<column>\" (the parent row's value for <column> \u2014 e.g. a plain-number parent key like a box's `number`, when the child table isn't a `ref`). Both tokens also resolve inside `toolbarActions[].action.args.values` (and anywhere else in this spec), so an inline \"+ add\" button can pre-fill the new child row's parent-key field.",B.f,null)
B.d1f=new A.q("expandPeek",B.X,"A HOST-COMPUTED detail line shown on the EXPANDED card face: { call, tapCall? } \u2014 `call` names a host query ([HostQuery], NOT a synced column) invoked with the row when the card expands; its returned text renders in muted secondary styling below the other expanded content, hidden while pending and hidden entirely when the result is null/empty. Optional `tapCall` names a second host query fired with the row when the line itself is tapped (e.g. open a detail page) \u2014 omit it for a non-tappable line. For read-only, per-viewer, or otherwise host-owned lookup data that must never be written into the board's synced tables (a dictionary lookup, a live status ping, \u2026); the engine never caches the result beyond the card staying expanded. Malformed/absent config renders nothing, byte-identical to before this prop existed.",B.f,null)
B.d59=new A.q("hideWhenEmpty",B.W,"Render nothing (no empty notice) when there are no cards \u2014 for a nested sub-thread that should stay invisible until it has rows.",B.f,null)
B.d7H=new A.q("autoEditNew",B.W,"Auto-open a freshly-added row expanded + in edit mode when a host flags it via board.settings[_autoEditRow] (e.g. add-to-thread drops a new empty card already editing). Gated to the row author.",B.f,null)
B.dbF=new A.q("addCard",B.X,'A tappable "add" card ({ label, icon?, action }) AFTER the last item, firing its action with no row \u2014 an inline add affordance that scrolls with the list. With an addCard the empty state is just the add card.',B.f,null)
B.d5J=new A.q("openIcon",B.D,"Under `editToolbar`, the row `open`/action surfaces as this top-right toolbar icon (default open_in_full) instead of a bottom button; the `open` label becomes its tooltip.",B.f,null)
B.dkB=new A.q("openActions",B.X,'Extra buttons beside the `open` button on an expanded card, each { label, icon?, action } fired with the row injected (e.g. "Show on map" \u2192 focusRow chained with goto). Ignored under `editToolbar`.',B.f,null)
