B.d86=new A.q("scopeRowId",B.D,"OPT-IN subtree scope (rehome-0804, mirrors `priolanes`' `scopeRowId`): a literal row id or a `$`-token (`$rowId`, `$selected:<table>`). Unconfigured (absent) leaves the card population byte-identical. Configured but UNRESOLVED (e.g. a `$selected:` token with nothing selected) fails CLOSED to the empty set \u2014 never falls back to the whole board. Configured + resolved keeps only rows reachable walking `scopeEdgesTable` DOWNWARD (contains edges) from the resolved row id; the root row itself is included.",B.f,null)
B.ui=new A.q("scopeEdgesTable",B.av,'With `scopeRowId`: the edges table to walk (default "relations").',B.f,null)
B.dfQ=new A.q("scopeEdgeFrom",B.v,'With `scopeRowId`: the edge\'s parent-id column (default "from" \u2014 matches `priolanes`\' own default; set explicitly when the edges table uses different column names, e.g. "fromId").',B.f,null)
