B.d34=new A.q("fill",B.W,'Fill the (bounded) parent and hand the active tab the remaining height via Expanded \u2014 needed when a tab hosts a height-filling surface (a bubl board, notepad, nested explorer, or a map/table/chart asking for height:"fill"). The active tab also republishes its own bounded height, so a height:"fill" child fills the TAB exactly (not the whole body) and pans internally. As a ROOT body it also takes the exact viewport height instead of the page-scroll fallback. Default off: segments shrink-wrap and drop into a scroll view.',B.f,null)
B.djZ=new A.q("chips",B.W,"Render the header as a compact row of small icon chips instead of full FilledButton text pills. Each segment map may carry an `icon` (a nav icon-name string, same registry as tab-bar icons); without one the chip falls back to the label's first letter in a small circle. The active chip is tinted, inactive chips are faint, and the current segment's label is shown next to the strip. Default off: the classic text-pill header (byte-identical to before this key existed).",B.f,null)
B.d7C=new A.q("swipe",B.W,"With `chips:true`, a horizontal drag ANYWHERE ON THE CHIP STRIP (never the body) advances/retreats the active segment, with an animated slide transition. Deliberately scoped to the strip \u2014 never a body-wide PageView \u2014 so a one-finger drag inside the active tab (a bubl board drag/marquee, an outline scroll, a canvas pan) is never intercepted. Default off.",B.f,null)
B.ddb=new A.q("transition",B.D,'With `swipe:true`, how the active tab\'s body animates on switch: "fade" (default) \u2014 a capped 150ms cross-fade, incoming child on top so a heavy outgoing child (a gantt, a big table) never reads as "stuck" over the new one \u2014 or "none" \u2014 an instant swap with no AnimatedSwitcher at all, for content sensitive to any transition cost. Ignored without `swipe:true`.',B.f,null)
B.d6G=new A.q("scrollBody",B.W,'The active tab\'s body scrolls INSIDE the bounded pane instead of being clipped, while the header/tab-bar stays docked above it \u2014 for a tab whose content (a list/column of rows) is naturally taller than the available slot. Implies `fill` (needs the same bounded pane); combine with a fixed screen/parent height, not with a child asking `height:"fill"` (that child would lose its bounded pane \u2014 use `fill` alone for that case). Default off: byte-identical to before this key existed.',B.f,null)
